# Email Service Configuration
# This file is for documentation purposes only
# Do not commit actual API keys to the repository

# EmailJS Configuration (example)
# Get your service ID, template ID, and public key from https://www.emailjs.com/
EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id
EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id
EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key

# Alternative: Resend API Key
# Get your API key from https://resend.com/
RESEND_API_KEY=your_resend_api_key

# Note: For the current implementation, the contact form uses a fallback
# that opens the user's email client when no service is configured.
# To enable server-side email sending, you would need to:
# 1. Sign up for EmailJS or Resend
# 2. Add your credentials to localStorage or implement a backend API
# 3. Update the Contact.razor component to use the configured service
